      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Sulfuric acid is soluble in water and hygroscopic, readily absorbing water vapour from the air. Anhydrous H2SO4 is a very polar liquid. It is highly corrosive to many materials and causes chemical burns on contact with the skin; it can badly burn cloth, plastic, rubber and injure the skin and eyes, so it must be handled with great care."
          },
